...@../../../dev/d2/themes/data
# Core state-authority boundary. Source findings and acceptance stay in Org.
title: ONE-USE AUTHORITY / STATE BEFORE EFFECT {
  class: title
  near: top-center
}
meaning: SCHEME / OWNED SEMANTICS {
  top: 0
  left: 0
  width: 370
  height: 650
  label.near: top-center
  style.font-size: 18
  style.fill: "#f7faf9"
  style.stroke: "#9bb6ad"
  policy: Admitted policy semantic root\nExpected operation / exact binding {
    top: 75
    left: 30
    width: 310
    height: 90
    class: semantic
  }
  context: Owner-derived validation context\nCurrent scoped spent membership {
    top: 270
    left: 30
    width: 310
    height: 90
    class: semantic
  }
  candidate: Pure transition candidate\nAccepted result is still inert {
    top: 465
    left: 30
    width: 310
    height: 90
    class: policy
  }
}
state: RUST / AUTHORITATIVE LEDGER {
  top: 0
  left: 500
  width: 440
  height: 650
  label.near: top-center
  style.font-size: 18
  style.fill: "#f8f9fc"
  style.stroke: "#a3abc0"
  brand: "" {
    shape: image
    icon: assets/rust.svg
    top: 14
    left: 14
    width: 30
    height: 30
  }
  snapshot: Execution root / revision / spent\nLineage / owner fence / revocation {
    top: 75
    left: 40
    width: 360
    height: 90
    class: ledger
  }
  cas: Commit exact snapshot / command\nVersion and unspent CAS / audit {
    top: 270
    left: 40
    width: 360
    height: 90
    class: runtime
  }
  spent: Committed one-use fact\nUnknown spends too / no handle yet {
    top: 465
    left: 40
    width: 360
    height: 90
    class: ledger
  }
}
execution: RUST / EXECUTION GUARDS {
  top: 0
  left: 1100
  width: 400
  height: 650
  label.near: top-center
  style.font-size: 18
  style.fill: "#f7f9fc"
  style.stroke: "#9cacc2"
  issuer: Original issuer positive consume\nBound logical operation / handoff {
    top: 75
    left: 30
    width: 340
    height: 90
    class: policy
  }
  obligations: Commit current obligations\nSource / history / held budget {
    top: 270
    left: 30
    width: 340
    height: 90
    class: ledger
  }
  gate: Typed unique claim / final gate\nExact peer / bytes / bounded range {
    top: 465
    left: 30
    width: 340
    height: 90
    class: runtime
  }
}
peer: Admitted external effect\nNo automatic replay {
  top: 465
  left: 1680
  width: 260
  height: 90
  class: ledger
}
restart: Restart / restore\nRecover facts / never local handles {
  top: 800
  left: 30
  width: 310
  height: 100
  class: ledger
}
resolve: Stale / duplicate / unknown commit\nResolve same command or quarantine {
  top: 800
  left: 540
  width: 360
  height: 100
  class: deny
}
recovery: Retain message recovery obligations\nNo pending replay / fresh-nonce bypass {
  top: 800
  left: 1130
  width: 340
  height: 100
  class: ledger
}
meaning.policy -> meaning.context
state.snapshot -> meaning.context: Authoritative projection
meaning.context -> meaning.candidate
meaning.candidate -> state.cas: Inert candidate / expected snapshot
state.cas -> state.spent: Spent monotone / revision advances
state.spent -> execution.obligations: Same canonical operation
execution.issuer -> execution.obligations
execution.obligations -> execution.gate
execution.gate -> peer: One bound effect
state.cas -> resolve: Conflict / lost reply
restart -> state.snapshot: Verified lineage / high-water
resolve -> recovery: Preserve uncertainty
rule: "Semantic root, execution root and state revision have different meanings. An unchanged execution root does not mean an unspent nonce.\nQuint models concurrent publication and restart. Lean preserves state/context alignment and logical-operation continuity under explicit physical premises." {
  shape: text
  class: note
  near: bottom-center
}

